The orthorhombic Y₂WO₆→Mn₂WO₆ analogue is the only physically usable high-ranking topology: after a 3.5% parent-cell contraction it places independent residual families at 19.81/20.39, 28.60, 34.77, 46.43, 51.60, 55.49–56.80, and 63.26° with a stable positive scale. Its parent intensities overpredict two low-angle reflections, so I’m following the requested topology-first route: bounded heavy-site coordinate refinement, then light sites only if Mn–O/W–O geometry remains physical.

