The three-phase model is now physically stable, with the broad residual family assigned to an Mn₂WO₆-type phase. I’m testing bounded microstrain and specimen terms from that checkpoint, then I’ll freeze the best replayable state and export the requested files.

The broadening test is still solving; the important safeguard here is that each bounded trial is recalculated after removing GSAS-II’s automatic bound freeze. That prevents a deceptively good, stale profile from being selected.

